//? Title: Bully Election: Which Responders Start an Election?
//? Subtitle: Actual static message traces, the preserved shortcut, and a quadratic responder cascade
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The highest live process id becomes coordinator, but that outcome alone does not
verify a bully-election message model. The original datamunge function contacts
all higher ids and then follows only the highest responder, so it runs at most
two candidate phases. We preserve its results and add an explicit static model
where every live higher responder starts an election once. The original six-node
example then has 11 versus 15 attempted messages. Native C++ supplies both
outcomes, actual send records, candidate phases, delivery flags and final learned
leaders. The report derives their different message counts and makes no claim
to simulate real network timing, partitions or the full original recovery protocol.
)

\toc

> Original six processes, with every live higher responder participating

Processes zero through five are known. Processes four and five are down, and
process one starts the election. In the full responder model, P1 contacts
P2, P3, P4 and P5. Live P2 and P3 each answer and activate once. P2 then
contacts P3, P4 and P5; P3 answers again but does not start a duplicate
candidate phase. Finally P3 contacts the two down higher ids, receives no
answer, and announces itself to P0, P1 and P2.

This is a fixed-liveness, three-message teaching model. Live destinations receive
logical messages reliably; failed destinations do not. Candidate processing uses
FIFO activation order, with higher targets visited in ascending id order. An
answer follows its delivered ELECTION immediately in the recorded sequence.
The diagram rows are actual send order, not elapsed time or network rounds.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bully_election_messages.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<char> alive{1,1,1,1,0,0};
  const auto trace=dm::algorithms::bully_elect_fanout_trace(6,alive,1);
  if (trace.result.leader!=3 || trace.total_messages!=15 || trace.delivered_messages!=9) return 1;
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(65,1100);
  for (int id=0;id<6;++id) {
    dm::graphics::DiagramStroke lifeline;lifeline.color={203,213,225};lifeline.dashed=true;
    diagram.path({{id*2.6,0.4},{id*2.6,-10}},lifeline);
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;style.width=1.2;style.height=1.0;style.padding=7;
    style.fill=!alive[id]?dm::RGB{226,232,240}:id==trace.result.leader?dm::RGB{220,252,231}:dm::RGB{239,246,255};
    diagram.node(std::format("p{}",id),{id*2.6,1.3},std::format("P{}\n{}",id,alive[id]?"up":"down"),style);
  }
  std::print("| send index | candidate phase | kind | sender | receiver | delivered |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for (std::size_t i=0;i<trace.messages.size();++i) {
    const auto& message=trace.messages[i];
    const bool election=message.kind==dm::algorithms::BullyMessageKind::Election;
    const bool answer=message.kind==dm::algorithms::BullyMessageKind::Answer;
    const std::string label=election?"E":answer?"OK":"C";
    const std::string name=election?"ELECTION":answer?"ANSWER":"COORDINATOR";
    const double y=-0.65*static_cast<double>(i);
    dm::graphics::DiagramStroke arrow;arrow.arrow=true;arrow.dashed=!message.delivered;
    arrow.color=election?dm::RGB{37,99,235}:answer?dm::RGB{22,163,74}:dm::RGB{217,119,6};
    diagram.path({{message.sender*2.6,y},{message.receiver*2.6,y}},arrow)
        .text({(message.sender+message.receiver)*1.3,y+0.19},label,15,arrow.color);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",i,message.phase,name,message.sender,message.receiver,message.delivered);
  }
  diagram.text({6.5,-10.6},"E = ELECTION; OK = ANSWER; C = COORDINATOR",16)
      .text({6.5,-11.2},"dashed arrows = down destination; rows show send order, not time",16)
      .save_svg("build/bully_election_messages.svg");
  std::print("\nWinner: P{}; attempted sends: {}; delivered sends: {}.\n",trace.result.leader,trace.total_messages,trace.delivered_messages);
  std::print("Final learned leader by id: {}.\n",trace.learned_leader);
}
```
