\caption(The trace includes failed contact attempts as dashed arrows. P0 sends no election messages but learns the coordinator from P3. Announcement phase three follows the three candidate phases and is not a fourth candidate.)
\alttext(Six process lifelines show fifteen arrows. P1 contacts P2 through P5, with answers from P2 and P3. P2 then contacts P3 through P5 and gets P3's answer. P3 contacts the two down nodes, then announces itself to P0, P1 and P2.)

Under the model's assumptions, every live id above the initiator is activated
by the initiator's first fanout. Each activates only once. The highest live
id L has no live higher responder and becomes the unique winner; every lower
candidate receives an answer from L and cannot win. All live lower ids learn
L from its announcement, including those below the initiator that never became
candidates. This argument depends on fixed liveness and successful delivery to
live destinations. The code obtains the winner from the actual no-responder
phase, rather than scanning for a maximum and attaching invented traffic.

> Preserve the original function and explain its different counts

The existing `bully_elect` API keeps the original highest-responder shortcut.
For this input it processes only P1 and P3. P2 answers P1 but never starts
its own election. Its recorded counts remain 6 ELECTION, 2 ANSWER and
3 COORDINATOR messages, exactly as in the original report. Those are valid
counts for the shortcut; they are not measurements of full responder fanout.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bully_election.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<char> alive{1,1,1,1,0,0};
  const auto shortcut=dm::algorithms::bully_elect_trace(6,alive,1);
  const auto fanout=dm::algorithms::bully_elect_fanout_trace(6,alive,1);
  std::print("| model | candidate phases | ELECTION | ANSWER | COORDINATOR | total attempts | delivered | winner |\n"
             "| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (const auto& [name,trace]:std::vector<std::pair<std::string,const dm::algorithms::BullyTrace*>>{
      {"legacy shortcut",&shortcut},{"all responders",&fanout}}) {
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",name,trace->rounds.size(),trace->result.election_messages,
        trace->result.answer_messages,trace->result.coordinator_messages,trace->total_messages,trace->delivered_messages,trace->result.leader);
  }
  std::print("\n| model | candidate | highest responder | contacts | answers | newly activated candidates |\n"
             "| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (const auto& [name,trace]:std::vector<std::pair<std::string,const dm::algorithms::BullyTrace*>>{
      {"shortcut",&shortcut},{"fanout",&fanout}})
    for (const auto& phase:trace->rounds)
      std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",name,phase.process,phase.highest_responder,
          phase.election_messages,phase.answer_messages,phase.candidates_started);
  if (shortcut.result.election_messages!=6 || shortcut.result.answer_messages!=2 || shortcut.total_messages!=11 ||
      fanout.result.election_messages!=9 || fanout.result.answer_messages!=3 || fanout.total_messages!=15) return 1;
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
      .bars({-0.18,0.82,1.82},{static_cast<double>(shortcut.result.election_messages),static_cast<double>(shortcut.result.answer_messages),
          static_cast<double>(shortcut.result.coordinator_messages)},"legacy shortcut",dm::RGB{37,99,235},0.36)
      .bars({0.18,1.18,2.18},{static_cast<double>(fanout.result.election_messages),static_cast<double>(fanout.result.answer_messages),
          static_cast<double>(fanout.result.coordinator_messages)},"all responders",dm::RGB{220,38,38},0.36)
      .x_tick_labels({"ELECTION","ANSWER","COORDINATOR"}).x_limits(-0.7,2.7).y_limits(0,11)
      .title("Original counts versus full responder fanout")
      .x_label("logical message category").y_label("attempted sends").size(1000,480)
      .save_svg("build/bully_election.svg");
}
