// result_end
\caption(The original three blue counts are retained. Red bars add the message work of P2's candidate phase. Both models elect P3, but identical leader outcomes do not imply identical protocol traffic.)
\alttext(Blue shortcut bars have heights six, two and three for election, answer and coordinator. Red full-responder bars have heights nine, three and three.)

The shortcut reaches the highest live responder directly after its first
candidate phase, then checks the remaining higher ids once more. Therefore
it has at most two candidate phases and linear message work. The previous
quadratic complexity claim did not describe this API's implementation.

> Derive the static counts and vary the initiator

Let n be the number of known ids, s the live initiator, L the highest live
id, and S the live ids greater than or equal to s. Put r=|S|. The fanout
model activates exactly S. A candidate p contacts every higher known id,
including down destinations. Each pair of distinct candidates contributes
one answer from the higher id to the lower id. Thus

\[
E=\sum_{p\in S}(n-1-p),\qquad
A=\frac{r(r-1)}2,\qquad C=L,\qquad M=E+A+C.
\]

C counts announcement *attempts* to every lower known id, rather than only
successful deliveries. If q live ids lie below L, delivered sends total
2A+q: A successful ELECTION deliveries, A answers and q announcements.
Down ids may affect E and C even though they never answer or activate.

For the shortcut, if s=L then E=n-1-L and A=0. Otherwise

\[
E=(n-1-s)+(n-1-L),\qquad A=r-1,\qquad C=L.
\]

With all nodes up and initiator zero, full fanout gives E=A=n(n-1)/2,
C=n-1 and M=n^2-1. The shortcut gives M=3(n-1). If the top process itself
initiates, both models have E=A=0 and M=n-1. Consequently an up top process
does not by itself imply an immediate or linear full-responder election:
*which process initiates* also matters.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bully_election_scaling.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::algorithms::BullyTraceOptions options;options.record_messages=false;
  std::vector<double> x,full,shortcut,top;
  std::print("| all-up n | fanout from P0: attempts | derived n^2-1 | shortcut from P0: attempts | fanout from top: attempts | full candidate phases | stored full messages |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (const std::size_t n:{2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512,1024}) {
    const std::vector<char> alive(n,1);
    const auto fanout=dm::algorithms::bully_elect_fanout_trace(n,alive,0,options);
    const auto legacy=dm::algorithms::bully_elect_trace(n,alive,0,options);
    const auto highest=dm::algorithms::bully_elect_fanout_trace(n,alive,static_cast<int>(n)-1,options);
    if (fanout.total_messages!=n*n-1 || legacy.total_messages!=3*(n-1) || highest.total_messages!=n-1 ||
        fanout.rounds.size()!=n || !fanout.messages.empty()) return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,fanout.total_messages,n*n-1,legacy.total_messages,
        highest.total_messages,fanout.rounds.size(),fanout.messages.size());
    x.push_back(std::log2(static_cast<double>(n)));
    full.push_back(std::log2(static_cast<double>(fanout.total_messages)));
    shortcut.push_back(std::log2(static_cast<double>(legacy.total_messages)));
    top.push_back(std::log2(static_cast<double>(highest.total_messages)));
  }
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
      .lines(x,full,"fanout, P0",dm::RGB{220,38,38},2).points(x,full,"",dm::RGB{220,38,38},4)
      .lines(x,shortcut,"shortcut, P0",dm::RGB{37,99,235},2).points(x,shortcut,"",dm::RGB{37,99,235},4)
      .lines(x,top,"fanout, top",dm::RGB{22,163,74},2).points(x,top,"",dm::RGB{22,163,74},4)
      .title("Initiator and responder policy determine message growth")
      .x_label("log2(number of processes n)").y_label("log2(actual logical send attempts)").y_limits(-1,25)
      .size(1100,520).save_svg("build/bully_election_scaling.svg");
}
```
