\caption(The program explicitly logs positive counts before plotting. Fanout initiated by zero approaches slope two; the shortcut and top-initiated fanout approach slope one. Lean tracing still executes and counts all sends, while omitting their O(M) individual records.)
\alttext(On base-two logarithmic axes, full fanout from zero grows quadratically, the shortcut from zero grows linearly at roughly three times the top-initiated linear count, and all three curves match their derived formulas.)

The kernel takes O(n+M) time for the fixed snapshot, with O(n) work storage.
Normal calls allocate no phase or message records. Full traces additionally
own O(n) candidate/learned-state records and O(M) send records; lean traces
retain O(n) records without changing M. Recording does not add a second
simulation. A finite send budget throws before exceeding its limit and never
returns a partial leader or trace.

> Boundaries, input checks and complete-call limits

Any nonzero liveness byte means up; unused entries beyond the requested
process count are ignored. An initiator must be live and in range. The
special initiator minus one means no election can start and is accepted only
for an all-down or empty prefix. A dead initiator cannot legitimately detect
a failure and run a protocol; the former unchecked indexing and fake activity
are replaced by explicit input errors.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  struct Example {std::string name;std::vector<char> alive;int initiator;};
  const std::vector<Example> examples{
      {"original two down",{1,1,1,1,0,0},1},
      {"all up, P0 initiates",{1,1,1,1,1,1},0},
      {"all up, P5 initiates",{1,1,1,1,1,1},5},
      {"only P1 up",{0,1,0,0,0,0},1},
      {"all down",{0,0,0,0,0,0},-1},{"empty",{},-1},{"one up",{1},0}};
  std::print("| case | leader | shortcut attempts | fanout attempts | fanout delivered | final learned leaders |\n"
             "| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for (const auto& example:examples) {
    const auto legacy=dm::algorithms::bully_elect_trace(example.alive.size(),example.alive,example.initiator);
    const auto full=dm::algorithms::bully_elect_fanout_trace(example.alive.size(),example.alive,example.initiator);
    if (legacy.result.leader!=full.result.leader) return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",example.name,full.result.leader,legacy.total_messages,
        full.total_messages,full.delivered_messages,full.learned_leader);
  }
  bool dead_initiator=false,short_flags=false,budget=false;
  try {(void)dm::algorithms::bully_elect_fanout(3,{1,0,1},1);}
  catch (const std::invalid_argument&) {dead_initiator=true;}
  try {(void)dm::algorithms::bully_elect(3,{1},0);}
  catch (const std::invalid_argument&) {short_flags=true;}
  dm::algorithms::BullyTraceOptions options;options.max_messages=14;options.record_messages=false;
  try {(void)dm::algorithms::bully_elect_fanout_trace(6,{1,1,1,1,0,0},1,options);}
  catch (const std::runtime_error&) {budget=true;}
  options.max_messages=15;
  const auto complete=dm::algorithms::bully_elect_fanout_trace(6,{1,1,1,1,0,0},1,options);
  if (!dead_initiator || !short_flags || !budget || complete.total_messages!=15 || !complete.messages.empty()) return 1;
  std::print("\nDead initiator, short liveness vector and fourteen-message cap rejected: {}, {}, {}.\n",
      dead_initiator,short_flags,budget);
  std::print("Exact fifteen-message cap succeeds with leader {}; stored individual messages: {}.\n",
      complete.result.leader,complete.messages.size());
}
```
